RED record: Cycle 002 audit accepts an unrelated failure reason
================================================================
Date: 2026-08-15
Pre-fix artifact: git blob b869852a (scripts/ms05_evidence_audit.py, Cycle 002)

The old fixture wrapper treats ANY AuditFailure as "failed as expected":

    def fixture_fails_as_expected(name, check):
        try:
            check()
        except AuditFailure as error:
            print(f"  fixture {name}: FAILED AS EXPECTED ({error})")
            return
        raise AssertionError(f"fixture {name} did NOT fail...")

There is no exact-code contract: a fixture that fails for the WRONG reason
(e.g. a missing required file instead of the intended hash mismatch) is still
reported as "FAILED AS EXPECTED". A wrong-reason fixture therefore passes.

New validator: each negative fixture must return its exact named error code;
an unrelated AuditFailure fails the fixture run.
